Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.ChargingPort.IsChargingCableLocked:
  comment: Locking of charging cable can be used to prevent unintentional removing during charging. True = Locked. False = Unlocked.
Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.ChargingPort.IsChargingCableConnected:
  comment: True = Connected. False = Not connected.
Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.ChargingPort.SupportedInletTypes:
  allowed: [
    'IEC_TYPE_1_AC',
    'IEC_TYPE_2_AC',
    'IEC_TYPE_3_AC',
    'IEC_TYPE_4_DC',
    'IEC_TYPE_1_CCS_DC',
    'IEC_TYPE_2_CCS_DC',
    'NACS_AC',
    'NACS_DC',
    'GBT_AC',
    'GBT_DC',
    'OTHER'
    ]
  comment:     A vehicle may have multiple charging ports.
               IEC_TYPE_1_AC refers to Type 1 as defined in IEC 62196-2.
               IEC_TYPE_2_AC refers to Type 2 as defined in IEC 62196-2.
               IEC_TYPE_3_AC refers to Type 3 as defined in IEC 62196-2.
               IEC_TYPE_4_DC refers to AA configuration as defined in IEC 62196-3. Also known as Type 4 or CHAdeMO connector.
               IEC_TYPE_1_CCS_DC refers to EE Configuration as defined in IEC 62196-3. Also known as CCS1 or Combo1 connector.
               IEC_TYPE_2_CCS_DC refers to FF Configuration as defined in IEC 62196-3. Also known as CCS2 or Combo2 connector.
               NACS_AC and NACS_DC refer to charging ports/methods based on NACS (North American Charging Standard).
               GBT_AC refers to connector specified in GB/T 20234.2.
               GBT_DC refers to connector specified in GB/T 20234.3. Also specified as BB Configuration in IEC 62196-3.
               OTHER shall be used for charging ports not included in the list above.
               For additional information see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEC_62196.
